{"availability":"available","full":"mmkon095/EV-INFRASTRUCTURE-MAPPING-USA","name":"EV-INFRASTRUCTURE-MAPPING-USA","description":"The goal of this Data Engineering project is to build an ETL pipeline that will help us assess the current state of Electric Vehicles (EV) infrastructure in the United States and map areas with inadequate charging station coverage.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2023-08-01T16:25:15Z","updated":"2026-07-14T01:10:40Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ev-infrastructure-mapping-usa-an5cmvr4onzywwnj8eqq6e.streamlit.app/","topics":["electric-vehicles","etl","ev","ev-infrastructure","geojson-data","pipeline","python","streamlit","streamlit-dashboard"],"demo":"https://ev-infrastructure-mapping-usa-an5cmvr4onzywwnj8eqq6e.streamlit.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T21:25:48.789Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T21:25:48.789Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T21:25:48.789Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T16:34:07.568Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T21:25:48.789Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["As the adoption of electric vehicles (EVs) continues to grow in the United States, the need for an efficient and well-distributed charging infrastructure becomes increasingly crucial. However, the expansion of EV charging stations has not been uniform across all regions, leading to potential infrastructure gaps that hinder the widespread adoption of electric vehicles. The goal of this Data Engineering project is to assess the current state of EV infrastructure in the United States and map areas with inadequate charging station coverage.","The Problem Involves the Following Key Objectives:","This project's findings and recommendations will have several benefits and implications:"],"features":["Data Collection: Gather comprehensive data on electric charging station locations, their capacities, and other relevant attributes from various sources, including public databases, charging station operators, and…","Electric Vehicle Ownership Data: Obtain data on electric vehicle ownership across different regions in the United States to understand the distribution and penetration of electric vehicles.","Geospatial Analysis: Perform geospatial analysis to visualize the distribution of existing charging stations and electric vehicle ownership on a map, identifying areas with high and low coverage.","Infrastructure Gap Identification: Utilize data analysis techniques to identify regions or areas that exhibit inadequate charging station coverage relative to the number of electric vehicles present.","Quantify the Impact of Gaps: Quantify the potential impact of infrastructure gaps on EV adoption rates and the overall transition to electric mobility in different regions."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mmkon095/EV-INFRASTRUCTURE-MAPPING-USA/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"da5d776892b997fd1e8cae9f60bf7fb9715b662bdadb8676b65b5997fda34c7d","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T16:34:07.735Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T16:34:07.735Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"As the adoption of electric vehicles (EVs) continues to grow in the United States, the need for an efficient and well-distributed charging infrastructure becomes increasingly crucial. However, the expansion of EV charging stations has not been uniform across all regions, leading to potential infrastructure gaps that hinder the widespread adoption of electric vehicles. The goal of this Data Engineering project is to assess the current state of EV infrastructure in the United States and map areas with inadequate charging station coverage.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mmkon095/EV-INFRASTRUCTURE-MAPPING-USA/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"da5d776892b997fd1e8cae9f60bf7fb9715b662bdadb8676b65b5997fda34c7d","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mmkon095/EV-INFRASTRUCTURE-MAPPING-USA/blob